@namespace Showcase.Web.Client.Pages

@page "/palette-switcher"

<DemoPageHeader Title="Palette Switcher" ComponentName="FaPaletteSwitcher" DocSlug="palette-switcher">
    Dropdown over all twenty-eight color palettes, plus your own additions — see also the
    <a href="/palette">Palette</a> section for a full swatch reference per palette, and
    "No picker at all" below for reskinning without any dropdown.
</DemoPageHeader>

<ComponentSubNav BaseRoute="/palette-switcher" />

<p>Already in this page's sidebar (top) — same component, dropped in again here:</p>
<div class="fa-demo-preview">
    <FaPaletteSwitcher />
</div>
<div class="fa-class-legend">
    <div class="fa-class-legend-row"><span class="fa-class-legend-label">Select</span><code>.fa-palette-switcher</code></div>
</div>
<div class="fa-code-block"><code>&lt;FaPaletteSwitcher /&gt;</code></div>

<h2 class="fa-mt-5">Adding your own palette</h2>
<p>
    Pass one or more <code>FaPalette</code> objects via <code>CustomPalettes</code> to
    append them after the twenty-eight built-ins. A custom palette has no compiled CSS
    of its own — its colors travel as JSON on the dropdown option and get applied as
    inline <code>--fa-*</code> custom properties on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> at
    selection time instead.
</p>
<div class="fa-demo-preview">
    <FaPaletteSwitcher CustomPalettes="_customPalettes" />
</div>
<div class="fa-code-block"><code>&lt;FaPaletteSwitcher CustomPalettes="_customPalettes" /&gt;

@@code {
    private readonly FaPalette[] _customPalettes =
    [
        new FaPalette(
            Value: "acme-brand",
            Label: "Acme Brand",
            Colors: new FaPaletteColors(
                Primary: "#2454ff", PrimaryDark: "#1638b0", PrimaryLight: "#7a9bff",
                Footer: "#eef1fb", Glow: "#3f6bff", Gold: "#d9a441", Accent: "#00a389",
                AccentDark: "#00786a", Ember: "#c0392b", Wine: "#6b1f2a", Fir: "#20242b",
                Cream: "#f7f8fc", Surface: "#ffffff", Text: "#1b1f2a", TextMuted: "#5c6270",
                TextOnPrimary: "#ffffff", Border: "#c9d2ec", BorderFocus: "#1638b0",
                AlertDangerBg: "#fbeaea", AlertSuccessBg: "#e3f5f1", AlertInfoBg: "#eaf0fc"),
            DarkOverrides: new FaPaletteDarkOverrides(
                Cream: "#14161d", Surface: "#1c1f29", Text: "#eef0f7", TextMuted: "#a3a9ba")),
    ];
}</code></div>
<p>See <a href="https://github.com/parrescence/FaFa/blob/dev/Blazor/docs/palette-switcher.md#adding-your-own-palettes">the full doc section</a> for what each color token maps to and the dark-mode-override caveat.</p>

<h2 class="fa-mt-5">No picker at all — plain CSS override</h2>
<p>
    Reskinning the whole app to one fixed brand doesn't need <code>FaPaletteSwitcher</code>
    or C# at all — every component reads color exclusively through the <code>--fa-*</code>
    custom properties <code>:root</code> defines, so redeclaring any of them in your own
    stylesheet, loaded after <code>fa-styles.css</code>, wins over whichever palette is
    active:
</p>
<div class="fa-code-block"><code>/* your-app.css, linked after fa-styles.css */
:root {
  --fa-primary: #2454ff;
  --fa-primary-dark: #1638b0;
  --fa-accent: #00a389;
  /* ...only the tokens you actually want to change */
}</code></div>
<p>
    See <a href="https://github.com/parrescence/FaFa/blob/dev/Blazor/docs/install.md#5-pick-a-color-palette-optional">Install &amp; setup, Option D</a>
    for the full token list and how this combines with a built-in or custom palette.
</p>

@code {
    private readonly FaPalette[] _customPalettes =
    [
        new FaPalette(
            Value: "acme-brand",
            Label: "Acme Brand",
            Colors: new FaPaletteColors(
                Primary: "#2454ff", PrimaryDark: "#1638b0", PrimaryLight: "#7a9bff",
                Footer: "#eef1fb", Glow: "#3f6bff", Gold: "#d9a441", Accent: "#00a389",
                AccentDark: "#00786a", Ember: "#c0392b", Wine: "#6b1f2a", Fir: "#20242b",
                Cream: "#f7f8fc", Surface: "#ffffff", Text: "#1b1f2a", TextMuted: "#5c6270",
                TextOnPrimary: "#ffffff", Border: "#c9d2ec", BorderFocus: "#1638b0",
                AlertDangerBg: "#fbeaea", AlertSuccessBg: "#e3f5f1", AlertInfoBg: "#eaf0fc"),
            DarkOverrides: new FaPaletteDarkOverrides(
                Cream: "#14161d", Surface: "#1c1f29", Text: "#eef0f7", TextMuted: "#a3a9ba")),
    ];
}